course: dictionary
lesson: 1196
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Bryony is a good example. Bryony with a small b is a climbing plant. Bryony with a capital B is a girl's name.
explain: Look at this sentence: «In Leeds, Bryony's baby brother was born early and is in hospital; Mum and Dad are there all the time and Bryony stays with Nan.» Bryony has a capital letter, it belongs to someone, and it stays with Nan like a person, so it is a girl's name.
explain: Now read: «The bryony climbed up the hedge, its red berries shining in autumn.» Climbed, hedge and berries are clues that point to the plant. Always ask what the word is doing in the sentence before you decide what it means.
fact: Bryony is a climbing plant found in hedges in Britain and Europe.
fact: There are two kinds: white bryony and black bryony.
fact: White bryony climbs using curly tendrils, and black bryony climbs by twisting its stems.
fact: Bryony has shiny red berries in autumn, and all parts of the plant are poisonous, especially the berries and roots.
fact: Bryony is also a girl's name, so it starts with a capital letter.
exercise: In «In Leeds, Bryony's baby brother was born early», what is Bryony? | A kind of hedge | A poisonous plant | A red berry | *A girl's name
exercise: «The bryony climbed up the hedge, its red berries shining in autumn.» What is bryony here? | *A climbing plant | A type of bird | A girl's name | A kind of rain
exercise: Why must you never eat bryony berries? | *Because they are poisonous | Because they only grow in summer | Because they are too big to chew | Because they taste bitter
test: Which kind of bryony climbs with curly tendrils? | *White bryony | Black bryony | Shiny bryony | Green bryony
test: In «Bryony stays with Nan», what kind of word is Bryony? | A berry | A plant | A hedge | *A name
exam: Which two words name the two kinds of bryony? | *White bryony and black bryony | Tendrils and berries | Bryony and Nan | Red bryony and green bryony
